### [Koka 3.2 Released](koka-3-2.html) {.blog-title}
**August 2025** · Language, Release

The 3.2 release introduces underscore syntax for concise eta-expansion, a more robust implicit resolving algorithm, and support for phantom implicits.

[Read more →](koka-3-2.html){.blog-read-more}

---

### [Koka 3.1 Released](koka-3-1.html) {.blog-title}
**July 2025** · Language, Release

The 3.1 release brings much faster build times via highly concurrent compilation, introduces the applier syntax and lazy constructors, and refines declaration syntax.

[Read more →](koka-3-1.html){.blog-read-more}

---

### [Koka 3.0 Released](koka-3-0.html) {.blog-title}
**January 2024** · Language, Release

The 3.0 release introduces experimental support for implicit parameters and locally qualified names, with major VS Code integration improvements.

[Read more →](koka-3-0.html){.blog-read-more}

---

### [Koka 2.6 Released](koka-2-6.html) {.blog-title}
**December 2023** · Language, Release

Koka 2.6.0 introduces first-class constructor contexts, expanded support for fully-in-place (FIP) programming, and initial VS Code language support.

[Read more →](koka-2-6.html){.blog-read-more}

